# `SEQUENCE-ORDER-MODEL`: the ORDER DERIVATION fixture. This genre's time axis is
# the `message` and `state` lines in the order they were written, the order is
# TOTAL, and NOTHING ELSE IN THE MODEL RECORDS IT — so what a second
# implementation must reproduce is the per-element `line` number and the array
# order that follows from it.
#
# The document is written so that a model which lost the order would still
# look plausible: the two collections INTERLEAVE, so `messages` and `states`
# each carry a non-contiguous run of line numbers and neither array alone is
# the trace. The trace is the union of the two sorted on `line`, and the
# golden is the only place that is checkable.
#
# The ids are deliberately NOT in alphabetical or any other order that a
# sorting implementation could accidentally reproduce.
figdown 0.4 sequence
title "Order is declaration order, and it is total"
lifeline z "Third column"
lifeline a "First column"
lifeline m "Second column"
message z -> a "1"
state a "OPEN"
message a -> m "2"
message m -> z "3"
state z "BUSY"
state a "CLOSED"
message z <- m "4"
state m "IDLE"
